    "text": "Consider the Bohr&#39;s model of a one-electron atom where the electron moves around the nucleus. In the following List-I contains some quantities for the <math><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow></msup></math> orbit of the atom and List-II contains options showing how they depend on <math><mi>n</mi></math> .<br />&nbsp;<table border=\"1px solid\">\t<thead>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<th><strong>List - I</strong></th>\t\t\t<th><strong>List - II</strong></th>\t\t</tr>\t</thead>\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(I) Radius of the <math><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow></msup></math> orbit</td>\t\t\t<td><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> <math><mo>&#8733;</mo><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(II) Angular momentum of the electron in the <math><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></math> orbit</td>\t\t\t<td><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> <math><mo>&#8733;</mo><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(III) Kinetic energy of the electron in the <math><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow></msup></math> orbit</td>\t\t\t<td><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> <math><mo>&#8733;</mo><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msup></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(IV) Potential energy of the electron in the <math><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow></msup></math> orbit</td>\t\t\t<td><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> <math><mo>&#8733;</mo><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> <math><mo>&#8733;</mo><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> <math><mo>&#8733;</mo><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><br />Which of the following options has the correct combination considering List-I and List-II?"
